# Gradle configuration cache artifacts (appear as shared/map(map(...)))
shared/map/

# Gradle / Kotlin Multiplatform
.gradle/
# Private Gradle user home created by ./gw (or direnv/.envrc). It holds the
# daemon registry, the native dir and .tmp/; the wrapper, caches and jdks
# entries inside it are symlinks to the real ~/.gradle.
# See docs/decisions/2026-10-04-gradle-daemon-isolation.md
/.gradle-user-home/
# Throwaway Gradle homes used to measure the daemon boundary. `gw` and
# .envrc create `.gradle-user-home` (ignored just above); a probe points
# GRADLE_USER_HOME at its own ad-hoc directory instead, and that directory is
# left behind holding a live daemon registry.
#
# The pattern covers the class rather than the one name that reached git:
# `.guh-probe-xyz/daemon/9.7.1/registry.bin` and its `.lock` were committed in
# 4c82ea8d — by the same commit that was adding this rule's neighbourhood. The
# `-xyz` suffix was chosen by whoever ran the probe, so pinning the exact name
# would ignore one directory and invite the next.
#
# A daemon registry is per-machine runtime state: a PID and a socket address,
# meaningful only while the daemon that wrote it is alive. It is never an input
# to a build, so there is nothing to gain by tracking it.
/.guh-probe-*/
build/
*.class
*.jar
# Wrapper jar must be committed for CI `./gradlew` to work — negation
# must come AFTER the blanket *.jar rule (last match wins in gitignore).
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
*.log

