**/build/
**/out/

# The OpenSpec spec tree is a source tree, not a build output. A capability
# under an area named `build` is a document the repository keeps, and the rule
# above drops it silently: the file is on disk, `git status` says the tree is
# clean, and the change it belongs to ships without a spec delta. The exception
# is narrow — only the spec directories, not the build directories themselves.
!openspec/changes/**/specs/build/
!openspec/changes/**/specs/build/**

# The published tree is the same tree: a capability that was archived lands in
# `openspec/specs/<area>/`, and `build` is one of the areas. Without this the
# published spec is on disk and in no commit, and the archive that produced it
# says the capability exists.
!openspec/specs/build/
!openspec/specs/build/**

