# Test results
**/test-results/
**/reports/
**/jvm-test-results/

# Allure results.
#
# The results live in `<module>/build/allure-results/`, and the build scripts
# say so with the `allure.results.directory` system property: the Allure 2.x
# JUnit listener reads it (`AllureLifecycle.getDefaultWriter()`) and falls back
# to a working-directory-relative `allure-results` only when the key is absent.
#
# The fallback is why this entry exists. A test task that does not set the
# property writes to `<module>/allure-results/` — outside `build/`, so the
# entries above did not cover it, and ~10k files sat untracked in `git status`
# after a local run. Every test task sets the property now; this line stays as
# the safety net that keeps a forgotten one from dirtying the working tree.
**/allure-results/

# KSP generated
**/ksp/

# Local Kiwi TCMS stand (infra/kiwi)
# TLS-ключ и самоподписанный сертификат — per-machine runtime state, как и
# volumes Postgres: коммитить их нельзя (секрет в репозитории), а генерируются
# они одной командой ./infra/kiwi/gen-tls.sh, которую вызывает up.sh.
infra/kiwi/tls/
infra/kiwi/secrets.env

