# Local env with secrets (API tokens, etc.)
.env
keystore/

# rumdl cache (local tool state)
.rumdl_cache/

# Python build metadata from `pip install -e scripts/src/`.
# scripts/src/sgate/sgate.egg-info was committed once and then contradicted the
# real project definition; the egg-info is regenerated on every install and must
# never be reviewed as source.
*.egg-info/

# Machine-local state written by the tooling that runs inside the checkout.
# The GitHub CLI keeps its own state under the XDG state directory. With no
# HOME to resolve that directory against, it falls back to a path relative to
# the working directory, so a `gh` call made from inside the checkout left
# `.local/state/gh/device-id` behind — and `git add` of the agent's working
# state carried it into a commit whose entire content was that one file.
#
# The pattern covers the class rather than the one name that reached git:
# `.local/` holds whatever the tooling wrote for this machine, and the next
# file under it is covered too. It is not anchored to the root, because the
# state directory is written wherever the tool that wrote it was standing.
#
# A state file is per-machine runtime state: meaningful only while the tool
# that wrote it is alive, and never an input to a build or a review. Nothing
# the repository needs lives under it, so there is nothing to gain by
# tracking it.
.local/
node_modules/
build-investigation/stage5-reports/full/
